我在塔吉特百货买了DVD，但我没有DVD播放机。

1005
00:38:49.770 --> 00:38:50.590
This is your problem.
这是你的问题。

1006
00:38:50.710 --> 00:38:53.250
You're very close to being able to enjoy this DVD.
你离能欣赏这张DVD只差一步之遥了。

1007
00:38:53.470 --> 00:38:53.750
I know.
我知道。

1008
00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:55.130
You're one major step away.
你只差关键的一步了。

1009
00:38:55.150 --> 00:38:55.530
I'm one major step.
我只差关键的一步。

1010
00:38:55.590 --> 00:38:58.030
I forgot we didn't have a DVD player anymore.
我忘了我们已经没有DVD播放机了。

1011
00:38:58.070 --> 00:38:59.070
So I have them.
所以我现在拿着它们。

1012
00:38:59.150 --> 00:39:03.710
But I read that there was a deleted scene where Devin, Devin, who sat in the background
但我读到过，有一个被删减的片段，德文，就是那个坐在背景里

1013
00:39:03.710 --> 00:39:06.750
with Creed, has a note card on his forehead.
和克里德坐在一起的德文，他额头上贴着一张索引卡。

1014
00:39:06.750 --> 00:39:07.650
And you see it.
你能看到它。

1015
00:39:07.770 --> 00:39:09.010
I think he's outside.
我想他在外面。

1016
00:39:09.010 --> 00:39:10.850
And as Michael walks in, he's outside.
当迈克尔走进来时，他在外面。

1017
00:39:10.850 --> 00:39:12.970
And his note card says, West Nile.
他的索引卡上写着“西尼罗河病毒”。

1018
00:39:14.370 --> 00:39:18.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

1019
00:39:18.320 --> 00:39:18.900
That's so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1020
00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:21.020
If you get a DVD player, will you come back and tell us?
如果你买了DVD播放机，你会回来告诉我们吗？

1021
00:39:21.020 --> 00:39:22.760
Yes, I've got to get to the bottom of that.
会的，我一定要弄清楚这件事。

1022
00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.000
I do want to talk about one scene.
我确实想聊聊其中一个场景。

1023
00:39:25.680 --> 00:39:30.260
Because when I put it out on Twitter that we were recording this episode, the most frequently
因为当我在推特上发布我们要录制这一集的消息时，被问到最多次的

1024
00:39:30.260 --> 00:39:35.400
asked question was about the scene where Mindy slaps Steve.
问题就是关于敏迪扇史蒂夫耳光的那场戏。

1025
00:39:35.720 --> 00:39:36.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1026
00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:39.100
People had a lot of questions about that scene.
大家对那场戏有很多疑问。

1027
00:39:39.580 --> 00:39:41.940
And I remember filming that.
我记得拍摄那场戏的情景。

1028
00:39:42.100 --> 00:39:45.900
And the reason I remember filming it is because Mindy could not stop laughing.
我之所以记得拍摄过程，是因为敏迪当时笑个不停。

1029
00:39:46.080 --> 00:39:47.140
Mindy could not stop laughing.
敏迪根本停不下来。

1030
00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:49.180
She laughed every single take.
她每一条都在笑。

1031
00:39:49.260 --> 00:39:49.820
Every take.
每一条都是。

1032
00:39:49.960 --> 00:39:52.120
And we were all standing there watching.
我们当时都站在旁边看着。

1033
00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:53.020
Yes.
是的。

1034
00:39:53.020 --> 00:39:58.500
And every time it was time for her to slap Steve, she would laugh.
每次轮到她扇史蒂夫耳光时，她就会笑。

1035
00:39:58.620 --> 00:40:01.400
But then right after she slapped Steve, she would laugh.
但就在她扇完史蒂夫之后，她还是会笑。

1036
00:40:01.640 --> 00:40:06.340
One thing we should say, and a lot of people wondered, was the slap real or fake?
有一点我们应该说明，很多人都很好奇，那一巴掌是真的还是假的？

1037
00:40:07.080 --> 00:40:09.320
Well, I remember we shot that so many times.
嗯，我记得我们拍了很多次。

1038
00:40:09.460 --> 00:40:11.700
And the majority of the time, it was fake.
大部分时候，那都是假的。

1039
00:40:11.740 --> 00:40:11.940
Fake.
假的。

1040
00:40:12.060 --> 00:40:12.480
It was fake.
那是假的。

1041
00:40:12.480 --> 00:40:13.760
She made no contact with him.
她根本没碰到他。

1042
00:40:13.840 --> 00:40:18.420
Because people wanted to know, oh my gosh, did he have a big red mark on his face or anything
因为人们想知道，天哪，他脸上有没有留下什么大红印之类的

1043
00:40:18.420 --> 00:40:18.980
like that?
东西？

1044
00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:23.160
But no, she, and thank goodness it was fake because she kept breaking every time.
但并没有，谢天谢地那是假的，因为她每次都忍不住笑场。

1045
00:40:23.400 --> 00:40:24.340
It was like unusable.
那简直没法用。

1046
00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:28.760
I feel like I do remember Steve, and I don't know if you remember this, Jenna.
我觉得我记得史蒂夫说过，不知道你还记不记得，珍娜。

1047
00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:32.660
I do feel like I remember him in one take saying, I think you, you know, just go ahead
我确实记得他在其中一条里说，我觉得你，你知道，干脆

1048
00:40:32.660 --> 00:40:33.340
and hit me once.
直接打我一下吧。

1049
00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:33.720
Yes.
是的。

1050
00:40:33.900 --> 00:40:34.820
Go ahead and hit me one time.
干脆直接打我一下吧。

1051
00:40:34.940 --> 00:40:35.100
Right.
没错。

1052
00:40:35.260 --> 00:40:38.000
So I think there was one where she made contact with him.
我觉得有一次她是和他接触了。

1053
00:40:38.140 --> 00:40:41.660
And there was also one time she didn't laugh.
还有一次她没笑。

1054
00:40:41.800 --> 00:40:43.200
And that's the time it's in the episode.
那一版被剪进了正片里。

1055
00:40:43.460 --> 00:40:43.740
That's it.
就是这样。

1056
00:40:43.860 --> 00:40:44.380
That's it.
就是这样。

1057
00:40:44.440 --> 00:40:48.400
But I think if you look really closely, you can see, I mean, we know Mindy.
但我觉得如果你仔细看，你能看出来，毕竟我们了解明迪。

1058
00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:48.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:40:48.820 --> 00:40:52.800
I think we, I can see her, her eyes are laughing a little bit.
我觉得我能看出来，她的眼睛里其实带点笑意。

1060
00:40:52.960 --> 00:40:56.000
Or she does a thing where she doesn't close her mouth all the way, and that's because she's
或者她有个习惯，就是嘴巴没完全闭上，那是因为她

1061
00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.680
about to laugh and she's trying not to.
快要笑场了，正在努力憋着。

1062
00:40:57.920 --> 00:40:58.460
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

1063
00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:04.020
We got to know each other all so well that I know everyone's tell before they break.
我们彼此太了解了，所以我知道每个人笑场前的征兆。

1064
00:41:04.140 --> 00:41:04.280
Yes.
没错。

1065
00:41:04.280 --> 00:41:07.140
Like, it's just so, like, clear when someone's about to laugh.
就比如，一个人快要笑场时表现得太明显了。

1066
00:41:07.320 --> 00:41:12.680
Another thing more than one person asked, I guess there's a controversy, is Steve saying
还有一件事，不止一个人问过，我想这算是个争议点，史蒂夫说的到底是

1067
00:41:12.680 --> 00:41:15.380
cookie cookie or googie googie?
“cookie cookie”还是“googie googie”？

1068
00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:16.720
He's saying googie googie.
他说的是“googie googie”。

1069
00:41:16.820 --> 00:41:17.440
Googie googie.
“googie googie”。

1070
00:41:17.620 --> 00:41:17.760
Yeah.
没错。

1071
00:41:17.760 --> 00:41:18.380
Yes.
是的。

1072
00:41:18.660 --> 00:41:20.380
Well, I'm glad we could solve that controversy.
好吧，很高兴我们解决了这个争议。

1073
00:41:20.400 --> 00:41:20.700
We cleared that up.
我们把它澄清了。

1074
00:41:21.140 --> 00:41:23.060
I have some note cards, m'lady.
我准备了一些卡片，女士。

1075
00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:24.780
Let's do a note card.
我们来读一张卡片吧。

1076
00:41:24.940 --> 00:41:25.160
Okay.
好的。

1077
00:41:25.520 --> 00:41:26.040
All right.
行。

1078
00:41:26.120 --> 00:41:29.740
This is a very sort of dorky actor moment, so just bear with me.
这算是一个很书呆子气的演员时刻，请大家多包涵。

1079
00:41:29.880 --> 00:41:35.940
But I thought John, as Jim, did such a fantastic job on the phone with Mr. Decker when he loses
我觉得约翰饰演的吉姆在和德克尔先生通电话，得知

1080
00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:37.160
his sale to Dwight.
销售机会被德怀特抢走时，表现得太棒了。

1081
00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:42.360
Oh, it is one of the hardest things in the world to have a fake one-sided phone conversation.
噢，进行一场虚假的单边电话对话是世界上最难的事情之一。

1082
00:41:42.360 --> 00:41:44.320
That has hills and valleys of emotion.
那段对话有着跌宕起伏的情绪。

1083
00:41:44.480 --> 00:41:44.640
Yes.
没错。

1084
00:41:44.720 --> 00:41:45.500
Where you're reacting.
你需要做出反应。

1085
00:41:45.800 --> 00:41:47.080
Like, he's excited.
比如，他先是兴奋。

1086
00:41:47.080 --> 00:41:48.020
Then he's disappointed.
然后感到失望。

1087
00:41:48.040 --> 00:41:49.980
Then he, like, figures out what happened.
接着他意识到发生了什么。

1088
00:41:50.040 --> 00:41:51.880
And there's no one on the other line.
而电话那头根本没人。

1089
00:41:52.140 --> 00:41:52.640
No one.
没人。

1090
00:41:52.880 --> 00:41:54.160
There's no one speaking to you.
没人跟你说话。

1091
00:41:54.280 --> 00:41:55.860
John is just doing that on his own.
约翰全靠自己演出来的。

1092
00:41:55.980 --> 00:41:56.120
Yes.
是的。

1093
00:41:56.120 --> 00:41:57.960
And I just sat there, and I rewatched it.
我当时就坐在那儿，又重看了一遍。

1094
00:41:58.020 --> 00:42:00.480
And, John, I just want you to know, you crushed that phone call.
约翰，我想让你知道，那段电话戏你演得太绝了。

1095
00:42:00.600 --> 00:42:01.760
You are so right.
你说得太对了。

1096
00:42:01.760 --> 00:42:08.220
Now, I have done films, or I have done things where someone is on the other line.
我拍过电影，或者做过一些戏，对方确实在电话那头。

1097
00:42:08.380 --> 00:42:14.080
For example, in season nine, when Pam breaks down crying at her desk, they figured out
比如在第九季，帕姆在办公桌前崩溃大哭时，他们想办法

1098
00:42:14.080 --> 00:42:18.920
a way to wire in John Krasinski live so I could hear him in my ear.
连线了约翰·卡拉辛斯基，这样我能通过耳机听到他的现场声音。

1099
00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:25.800
So there are times when there's a really emotional scene or a scene that really requires you to
所以有些时候，如果是一场非常情绪化的戏，或者确实需要你

1100
00:42:25.800 --> 00:42:26.820
speak to the other actor.
和对方演员对话的戏，就会这样做。

1101
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:30.500
But, like, 90% of the time, you are just pretending someone is there.
但有百分之九十的时间，你只是在假装有人在那儿。

1102
00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:31.140
There's no one there.
其实根本没人。

1103
00:42:31.140 --> 00:42:32.320
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1104
00:42:32.720 --> 00:42:35.960
And so John was just talking to Mr. Decker, who wasn't there.
所以约翰当时只是在跟根本不在场的德克尔先生说话。

1105
00:42:36.120 --> 00:42:37.660
And I just thought he did such a great job.
而我觉得他演得太棒了。

1106
00:42:37.860 --> 00:42:40.940
So anyway, I just had to give a little love to J.K.
总之，我一定要给J.K.一点赞赏。

1107
00:42:41.540 --> 00:42:41.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1108
00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:48.980
And after that scene, when Jim finds out that he has lost the sale, that Dwight stole the
在那场戏之后，当吉姆发现他丢了那笔生意，发现德怀特抢走了

1109
00:42:48.980 --> 00:42:54.180
sale that is 25% of his income, he goes back into the conference room where Michael is
那笔占他收入百分之二十五的生意时，他回到会议室，迈克尔正在

1110
00:42:54.180 --> 00:42:56.940
wrapping things up, and everyone is bored to tears.
做总结，大家都无聊透顶了。

1111
00:42:56.940 --> 00:43:01.300
And that is when Pam falls asleep on Jim's shoulder.
就在那时，帕姆靠在吉姆的肩膀上睡着了。

1112
00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:09.840
And we filmed that about, oh, my goodness, like 15, 16 times, that scene.
那场戏我们大概拍了，天哪，拍了十五六次吧。

1113
00:43:10.080 --> 00:43:13.720
Because this was our Jim-Pam moment of the episode.
因为这是这一集里属于吉姆和帕姆的时刻。

1114
00:43:13.720 --> 00:43:14.820
This was it.
就是这一刻。

1115
00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:19.180
And they really wanted to get these little Jim-Pam moments just perfectly.
他们真的想把这些吉姆和帕姆的小瞬间拍得尽善尽美。

1116
00:43:19.480 --> 00:43:24.740
I looked up this scene in the script, and there is a piece of stage direction that BJ Novak
我在剧本里查了这场戏，有一段舞台指示是B.J.诺瓦克

1117
00:43:24.740 --> 00:43:28.640
wrote that I want to read for you because I think it is so perfect.
写的，我想读给你们听，因为我觉得写得太完美了。

1118
00:43:28.640 --> 00:43:36.080
He wrote, Jim reacts to Pam falling asleep on him like a butterfly has landed on his shoulder.
他写道：吉姆对帕姆靠在他身上睡着的反应，就像有一只蝴蝶落在了他的肩膀上。

1119
00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:37.360
Aww.
噢。

1120
00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:39.000
Isn't that so poetic?
这不是很诗意吗？

1121
